# Common layer

Root `lib/` is shared by every target. Platform widgets belong in `lib/mobile/`, `lib/web/`, or `lib/desktop/`. Folder roles: `apps/reader_flutter/lib/CLAUDE.md`.

## Rules

- One implementation for data, auth, sync, and business rules (`providers/`, `models/`, `storage/`, `security/`).
- Common code does not import `lib/mobile/`, `lib/web/`, or `lib/desktop/`.
- `lib/utils/` has no `BuildContext` and no platform UI.
- `lib/screens/` are route adapters. They wire providers and branch web → desktop → mobile. Mobile is the unguarded fallthrough. When a mobile branch is still an inline `Scaffold` in `lib/screens/`, move it to `lib/mobile/` as part of the edit.
- Strings live in both `app_en.arb` and `app_am.arb`. Read them with `AppLocalizations.of(context)`.
- Brand tokens: `AppColors`, `AppSpace`, `AppRadius`, `AppTheme.light` (the only theme). Web and desktop extend them with `WebTokens` and `DesktopTokens`. Mobile uses the shared tokens directly.
- Offline book bytes go through `BookCrypto` and `SecureBookStore`. Plaintext content, the master key, and licenses stay off disk.
- Authenticated HTTP uses `apiDioProvider`.

```dart
if (useWebShell(context)) {
  return const WebPageScaffold(body: HomeScreenBody());
}
if (useDesktopShell(context)) {
  return const DesktopPageScaffold(body: DesktopHomeScreenBody());
}
return const MobileHomeScreen();
```
